    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i guess. but \"fleeting brilliance\" feels like a consolation prize for a losing game. it just feels like we're putting in all this work—dealing with pain, loss, and just the daily grind—to build something that's destined to be erased. if the end result is just zero, then the struggle itself feels kind of irrational, doesnt it? like we're just wasting energy for no reason.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
