    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk, i just can't see it that way. it feels more like we're just fighting against the inevitable. if you know for a fact that every single thing you build is going to be destroyed by entropy, why bother putting in the energy to build it in the first place? it feels more logical to just... not participate. to just stop the cycle of depletion before it consumes everything. does it really make sense to keep pushing when the math says it's all going to zero anyway?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
